\label{conj8999}
For every integer $m \geq 2$, one has $$\mathsf{D} (\llbracket -m,m \rrbracket ^2) =4m^2-q(m).$$ 
Moreover, up to symmetries and reordering of terms, $S(m)$ is the only minimal zero-sum sequence of maximal length over $\llbracket -m,m \rrbracket ^2$.

\label{thmbox3}
For every integer $m \geq 2$, one has
$$
\mathsf{D}^{(4)} ( \llbracket -m,m \rrbracket ^3) \geq 
\left\{
\begin{array}{ll}
16m^3 - 16m^2 +10m-2 	& {\mathrm{ if }}\ m\  \mathrm{ is\ odd,} \\
16m^3 - 16m^2 +8m-1 	& \mathrm{ if }\ m\  \mathrm{ is\ even.}
\end{array}
\right.
$$
